 "text": "9/29/26, 9:47 AM\nFirst you restrict the archiving volume. To do this, enter the ID of the TOU exception program for which you want the TOU\nexceptions to be archived.\n\ne Determination of Final Date for Archiving:\n\nThe retention period in days in defined in Customizing for SAP Utilities under |*Tools \u00bb Archiving \u00bb Define Retention\nPeriod for Archiving Objects %. The system determines the final date for archiving from this retention period. You can only\narchive documents whose existence exceeds the retention period defined in Customizing. The system uses the retention\nperiod for the archiving object ISU BILL (billing document header) to determine the final date for archiving TOU\nexceptions.\n\ne Determine Billing Documents:\nTOU exceptions can only be archived if the billing documents for the corresponding TOU exception have been archived.\ne Determine the TOU Exception Responses\n\nTOU exceptions can only be archived if the TOU exception responses for the corresponding TOU exception have been\narchived.\n\ne Write Temporary Index:\n\nThe system writes the TOU exception ID and the TOU exception program to the index table ETOUEXCEPTIONAR for the\nTOU exceptions that can be archived. This index table is used as the basis for archiving. Once data has been successfully\narchived and deleted, the system deletes the respective index entry from the database.\n\n2. Archiving of Selected TOU Exceptions (Report REAARCH_ARCH_EXCEPT)\n\nPrerequisite\nBefore starting this archiving report, you must perform at least one analysis using the REAARCH_ ANALYSE EXCEPT report.\nProcess Flow\n\nThe archiving report selects TOU exceptions for which a corresponding entry exists in the index table ETOUEXCEPTIONAR, whose\nentries are generated by the analysis report. The system writes the entries found to the archive.\n\n1 Note\n\nIf you start the report in the test mode, the system does not write the data to the archive, and only displays an overview of the\nTOU exceptions that you can archive (if a detailed log display is required).\n\nWhen you start the report you can make various settings on the initial screen:\n\ne Archiving\n\nYou can use this action to archive data for completed business objects. The system performs archivability checks to\nestablish whether data can be archived. In this regard, this function is the same as standard data archiving. The ILM\nenhancements mean that during the write phase, the system can evaluate the rules maintained in the Information\nRetention Manager (IRM) for each object instance and therefore determine the retention period and the storage location\nfor the object. This information is persisted to the database as part of the administration data and is interpreted later\nduring storage.\n\ne Snapshots\n",
